1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
DappGo existed before this hackathon.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:06,466
Everything here was built
from October 27 to November 4.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,666
A finance post goes viral.

4
00:00:09,666 --> 00:00:10,966
Thousands repost it.

5
00:00:10,966 --> 00:00:11,733
Is it right?

6
00:00:11,733 --> 00:00:15,000
This one has a real number
— and the wrong period.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,666
Numbers like this move money,
and wrong numbers lose it.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,566
And it's not just text.

9
00:00:21,566 --> 00:00:22,400
Screenshots,

10
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:25,433
PDFs, podcasts, videos
— numbers everywhere.

11
00:00:25,433 --> 00:00:27,466
How do you check all of them?

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,800
Asking a model directly
gets one in five right.

13
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,533
Give the same model SEC evidence,
and let a program decide:

14
00:00:39,533 --> 00:00:40,466
nine in ten —

15
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,866
on held-out claims, 240 of 266.

16
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,500
Meta's Muse Spark extracts each
claim and picks the SEC lookup.

17
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,133
Python does the arithmetic
and returns the verdict.

18
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:57,300
Model proposes; program decides.

19
00:01:00,233 --> 00:01:01,700
Live, on the site.

20
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:02,966
Paste the post.

21
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:07,766
Muse Spark calls the SEC tools.

22
00:01:21,566 --> 00:01:23,433
Contradicted, with the filing.

23
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:26,233
And here is the corrected draft.

24
00:01:28,433 --> 00:01:35,333
Apple's annual revenue was $416
billion; the quarter was $102.5 billion.

25
00:01:36,566 --> 00:01:38,700
Every SEC call is on the record.

26
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:40,200
You can see each call.

27
00:01:50,533 --> 00:01:52,166
Cost and time, on the receipt.

28
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,866
The same checks run in batch
from the command line — text,

29
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,333
screenshots through Muse OCR,

30
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,400
audio through Muse Voice Transcribe.

31
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,933
On saved Threads posts,
the median was 6.8 seconds.

32
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:15,833
At that median, a thousand posts
take about two hours on one worker.

33
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,133
Ninety point two percent
on held-out claims.

34
00:02:21,133 --> 00:02:24,000
It wrongly says 'supported' once in 139.

35
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,433
Two cents and ten seconds a claim.

36
00:02:26,433 --> 00:02:30,800
On real posts, coverage is
reported separately from accuracy.

37
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,833
Every number, checked against the filing.

38
00:02:36,833 --> 00:02:38,900
hackathon dot dappgo dot com.

39
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,033
Built with Meta Muse Spark, on Baseten.

40
00:02:53,033 --> 00:02:53,600
DappGo.

